{#
   The Scout mark. `size` is the rendered edge in px (default 76).

   SVG (2026-08-14), traced from the raster by `brand-src/gen_scout_logo.py`:
   4 kB where the 500x500 JPG was 104 kB, and crisp at any pixel density
   instead of a fixed 500 px master shown at 64-80. A pin, three rings and a
   wordmark in two flat colours is the art JPEG compresses worst and vector
   describes best. The orange tile is part of the file, so the two pages that
   include this are unchanged — taking the tile off (a `<rect>` in the SVG) is
   a one-line change whenever the dark hero wants the mark bare.
#}
{% set size = size|default(76) %}
<img class="scout-logo" src="{{ asset('brand/scout-logo.svg') }}" alt="{{ 'scout.logo_alt'|trans }}"
     width="{{ size }}" height="{{ size }}" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
     style="width:{{ size }}px;height:{{ size }}px">
